  "description": "🎵 <em>This experience is brought to you by </em><strong><em>Belmont Ensemble</em></strong><em>. This concert is not affiliated with the Fever Original Candlelight series.</em><br><em>Seating is unreserved and allocated on arrival. Concession ticket holders may be seated in either the ground floor or balcony sections (but not Front Row).&nbsp;</em><br><br><strong>Highlights</strong><br> 🌙 London's finest musicians perform Gershwin's Rhapsody in Blue and other classical favourites<br> 🏛️ The perfect option for first-time classical concert-goers<br> ⛪ The beautiful Bloomsbury Central gently lit by candlelight<br><br><strong>General Info</strong><br> 📅 Dates and times: select your date and time directly in the ticket selector&nbsp;<br> ⏳ Duration: 1 hour. Doors open 30 minutes before the concert starts<br> 📍 Location: Bloomsbury Central, 235 Shaftesbury Avenue, London&nbsp;<br> 👤 Age requirement: 6+&nbsp;(Concession children tickets are available for under 18 years old.)<br><br><strong><u>Programme :</u></strong><br><br><ul><li><strong>Saturday 19 September and 17 October at 5pm and 7:30pm</strong></li><li><strong>Saturday 26 December at 3pm and 5:30pm</strong></li><li>Gershwin - Rhapsody in Blue</li><li>Beethoven - 'Moonlight' Sonata</li><li>Mozart - Piano Sonata in C Major K.545</li><li>Ravel - Ondine from Gaspard de la nuit</li><li><em>Viktor Erik Emanuel - Piano</em></li></ul><br><strong>Description</strong><br>Brought to you by <em>Belmont Ensemble</em>, immerse yourself in the enchanting world of classical music at London's Bloomsbury Central Baptist Church, gently lit by candlelight. Perfect for first-time classical concert-goers, this unforgettable evening features London's finest musicians performing Gershwin's dynamic 'Rhapsody in Blue' and other timeless favourites. From Gershwin's dazzling 'Rhapsody in Blue' to Beethoven's 'Moonlight' Sonata, from Mozart's haunting Rondo to Chopin's exquisite Nocturnes, let the music transport you to a realm of pure elegance and beauty. Get your tickets now for <em>Rhapsody in Blue by Candlelight on Shaftesbury Avenue</em>, in the heart of London's famous Theatre District!<br>",
